    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0395" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg307"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Mr.
                            Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Newport</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1892-09-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                    1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    forwarded to the governor-general of Canada a copy of your note of the 2d
                    August, in which you point out that the President of the United States is
                    powerless to issue his proclamation putting the act of Congress in regard to
                    wrecking and salvage privileges in the inland waters contiguous to Canada and
                    the United States into force until the Canadian Government, by construction of
                    their recent act on the same subject, or otherwise, can give him the assurance
                    that the wrecking and salvage privileges granted by the Dominion shall apply to
                    the waters specially mentioned by act of Congress, so far as they lie within the
                    Dominion of Canada.</p>
                <p>I have now received a communication from his excellency in reply, forwarding copy
                    of an approved minute of council on the subject, from which it appears that the
                    Canadian Government are unable to give the necessary assurance until they are
                    empowered to do so by act of Parliament.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Michael H.
                    Herbert.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d250-a1.xml" xpointer="d250-a1"/>
            </div>
